<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Ammar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1031–1086</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Abu Bakr ibn Ammar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Ammar was an Andalusi poet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silves">Silves</a> and the friend and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of al-Mutamid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>. He accompanied al-Mutamid as governor of Silves and in 1078 took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> for Seville, but then ruled it in defiance of his master. Captured, he was imprisoned and killed by al-Mutamid in 1086.</p></div>
